{
  "case_id": "2016-16-5294",
  "document_hash": "7d518b92c0ea68e3f6accbd8146940140d4f098880cdad73330a6d2739ee2d13",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-16-5294",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d518b92c0ea68e3f6accbd8146940140d4f098880cdad73330a6d2739ee2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d518b92c0ea-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument\nfirst this morning in Case 16-5294, McWilliams v. Dunn."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-16-5294",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d518b92c0ea68e3f6accbd8146940140d4f098880cdad73330a6d2739ee2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d518b92c0ea-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "WHERE, SOMEWHERE ELSE, DOES IT BECOME APPARENT THAT HE WANTS THE STATE TO APPOINT AN EXPERT? WHERE? I JUST WANT TO KNOW WHERE."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of Alabama",
      "case_id": "2016-16-5294",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d518b92c0ea68e3f6accbd8146940140d4f098880cdad73330a6d2739ee2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d518b92c0ea-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State argues he got everything he's entitled to under Ake, a neutral expert. He's not entitled to any more."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McWilliams",
      "case_id": "2016-16-5294",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d518b92c0ea68e3f6accbd8146940140d4f098880cdad73330a6d2739ee2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d518b92c0ea-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The argument for -- on behalf of Mr. McWilliams was that he was entitled to an independent expert."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-5294",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d518b92c0ea68e3f6accbd8146940140d4f098880cdad73330a6d2739ee2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d518b92c0ea-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "both the State of Alabama and the defendant brief it on the merits of the Ake claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-16-5294",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d518b92c0ea68e3f6accbd8146940140d4f098880cdad73330a6d2739ee2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d518b92c0ea-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Suppose the Judge, the court, appoints the head of the psychiatric department at a distinguished private university, one person, and he comes in and he tells the defense counsel, now I'm going to explain to you what all these terms mean."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-5294",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d518b92c0ea68e3f6accbd8146940140d4f098880cdad73330a6d2739ee2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d518b92c0ea-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Sorry, General, but if we could just focus on -- because I think it would help to just sort of -- let's assume for the moment that this defendant did not get what he was asking for, which was a defense expert, and say whether Ake entitled him to such an expert."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-16-5294",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d518b92c0ea68e3f6accbd8146940140d4f098880cdad73330a6d2739ee2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d518b92c0ea-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Is there -- is there any jurisdiction that holds that today, that all that Ake requires is a neutral expert? I thought by now every jurisdiction recognizes that Ake requires an expert who will be, essentially, part of the defense team."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-16-5294",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d518b92c0ea68e3f6accbd8146940140d4f098880cdad73330a6d2739ee2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d518b92c0ea-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, if Ake says that you have a right to meaningful assistance from a -- from a psychiatrist, you, the defense, and then over time it becomes clear to us that that psychiatrist must be -- must -- must be retained for the benefit of the defense only, is that a new clearly established holding, or is it simply a refinement of a clearly established right that was set forth in Ake?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2016-16-5294",
      "confidence": 0.0,
